\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Point-estimate regime between folded and original TorchInductor. ``Fold dominates'' means lower mean fixed cost (including preprocessing) and no higher mean execution; ``fold until \(n\)'' means that the original point-estimate line becomes lower after \(n\). No input yields a finite boundary under the \(K=5\) point estimates.}}{7}{figure.caption.22}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:foldeq}{{4}{7}{Point-estimate regime between folded and original TorchInductor. ``Fold dominates'' means lower mean fixed cost (including preprocessing) and no higher mean execution; ``fold until \(n\)'' means that the original point-estimate line becomes lower after \(n\). No input yields a finite boundary under the \(K=5\) point estimates}{figure.caption.22}{}}
